Subject: Lift the 255-argument call limit

What this does
  Lift the 255-argument call limit.

Why we need it
  A call, method call or construction with more than 255 arguments -- legal JavaScript, and what a template with many substitutions compiles to -- was refused because the call opcodes' argument count is one byte and the analysis simulator's operand array was fixed at 258.

What it adds
  `JSRegStepEv.pop` points at a caller-provided buffer sized to the deepest operand stack; calls with `argc > 255` build an arguments array in 255-value chunks (`ROP_array_from` + `ROP_append`) and go through `ROP_apply`; a `JSRegIR.big_args` flag reserves the 262 window slots the sequence stages through.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
